From 92b9ff4c3ae967ea1af7669c7a847b0b2b9e09cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaan <kaan@local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:31:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add boot diagnostics: reset reason, boot count, previous run
 length (fw 2.4.6)

Surfaces why the board reset, readable from the phone with no serial
console attached. Added because the board runs for a while then resets
on the mains supply and the cause is unknown.

Firmware:
- captureBootDiag() runs first in setup() so nothing obscures the reason
- esp_reset_reason() mapped to a short label (BROWNOUT, PANIC, WDT, etc)
- RTC_NOINIT_ATTR counters survive a reset, guarded by a magic word so a
  genuine cold boot is distinguishable from a warm one
- live uptime ticked into RTC memory each second, so after a reset the
  previous run length is known
- telemetry gains rst, boots, lastrun, minheap; buffer grown 640 to 768

Web GUI (Help panel diagnostics dump):
- new line: last reset reason, boot number, previous run length
- free heap line now also shows the minimum ever seen (catches a leak)
- plain-language hint explaining what each reset reason implies
---
 kinetic_sculpture.ino | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 page.h                | 15 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

